{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/1vfd37","slideIndex":2,"text":"Sources: DuplicateQuestion_MaLSTM/model.py and ensemble.py. Three independent models use Google News, FastText Crawl, and FastText Subword embeddings. Each model shares its embedding layer and LSTM across the two question branches. Embeddings are frozen. LSTM has 50 units. Thirty epochs is inferred from the paper plots. LSTM units, optimizer, loss, and batch size are implementation choices. A raw score is a similarity score used for binary prediction and need not be a calibrated probability."}
