{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/5qjr0x","slideIndex":4,"text":"Source: DuplicateQuestion_MaLSTM/results/tuned/comparison.csv and ensemble.py. Original blend weights: 0.33 Google, 0.33 FastText, 0.34 Subword. Isotonic weights: 0.30/0.45/0.25 and threshold 0.48. Validation selects isotonic blending. Its test accuracy gain is 0.539214 percentage points. Stacking achieves 82.3563 test accuracy but was not selected by validation. Calibration Brier score falls from 0.1341055 to 0.1273568, lower is better. Half the validation data fits calibration/stacking and half selects weights and thresholds. Original test metrics were already inspected, so extensions are exploratory. Paper reports 91.14%, which this project did not reproduce."}